  requiredFlags: []
  blockedFlags: []
  speaker: 3
  text: 'The gate closes. The dawn is ordinary and enormous.


    The box is not
    full. She can name the missing pieces - which is its own kind of remembering
    - and the pieces she has, she has read aloud, checked, and corrected, the way
    her mother taught her to study.


    Some of the voice is gone. Not all of it.
    Never all of it.


    She carries the box home the way you carry a lit lamp
    through wind: close, and careful.'
  localizationKeys:
  - PARTIAL MEMORY
  - She saved what she could hold. Some of the voice is gone; not all of it.
